 "stimulus_html": "<figure id=\"Ch16_fig06\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/0068ea5d134d8ad2.png\" alt=\"A line graph shows the Temperature of the Earth in Celsius over a span of time between 1880 and the 2000s. Numbers from the following four sources are shown: NASA Goddard Institute for Space Studies, Met Office Hadley Centre/Climatic Research Unit, NOAA National Climatic Data Center, and Japanese Meteorological Agency. The sources have negligible differences in their information. The temperature has minor fluctuations but follows this pattern: From 1880 to the late 1930s, the temperature stays below 0 degrees, hovering around –0.25. From the late 1930s to the late 1970s, the temperature stays around 0 degrees. From the late 1970s to the late 2000s, the temperature steadily rises until plateauing around 0.50 degrees.\">\n<figcaption>NASA graph showing Earth’s temperature anomalies since 1880. (credit: “Earth Temperature” by Bill of Rights Institute/Flickr, CC BY 4.0)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><i>Refer to the chart provided.</i></p>",
